// Markup showcase
//
// Demonstrates inline markup tags. Tags are stripped from the display text;
// the TUI uses the resulting span metadata to apply terminal styling.
//
// Run:
//   cargo run -p bubbles-tui -- examples/snippets/markup.bub
//
// Supported tags in bubbles-tui:
//   [b]text[/b]              bold
//   [i]text[/i]              italic
//   [u]text[/u]              underline
//   [dim]text[/dim]          dim
//   [em]text[/em]            italic (alias)
//   [color value=NAME]...[/color]   coloured text (red, green, yellow, blue,
//                                   cyan, magenta, white, gray, and their
//                                   light* variants)
//   [pause /]                self-closing; no visible text, zero-length span

title: Markup
---
Narrator: [b]Bold[/b], [i]italic[/i], and [u]underline[/u] — the essentials.
Narrator: Combine them: [b][i]bold-italic[/i][/b], or [u][i]underlined italic[/i][/u].
Narrator: Use [dim]dim text[/dim] for parenthetical asides.
Narrator: [color value=red]Danger![/color] [color value=green]All clear.[/color] [color value=yellow]Proceed with caution.[/color]
Narrator: Mix markup and {$mood} together freely.

<<declare $mood = "caution">>

Narrator: How do you feel about that?

-> [b]Excited![/b] Let's go.
    Narrator: [color value=green]That's the spirit.[/color] Off you go.
-> [dim]Cautiously optimistic...[/dim]
    Narrator: Wise. [i]Very[/i] wise.
-> [color value=red]Terrified.[/color]
    Narrator: Understandable. Take a [u]deep breath[/u] first.
===
